138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 50 0 R
/T (Example: If driver details were stored only in BOOKING, deleting the driver's last booking could also remove the only stored copy of that driver's name and phone number. Likewise, if a customer's profile were stored only alongside bookings, deleting the customer's last booking could erase the profile. Keeping CUSTOMER and DRIVER as separate tables helps prevent this. Deleting a booking should not automatically delete the associated customer, driver, or cab master record. Foreign-key deletion rules should be chosen carefully.)
/E (Example: If driver details were stored only in BOOKING, deleting the driver's last booking could also remove the only stored copy of that driver's name and phone number. Likewise, if a customer's profile were stored only alongside bookings, deleting the customer's last booking could erase the profile. Keeping CUSTOMER and DRIVER as separate tables helps prevent this. Deleting a booking should not automatically delete the associated customer, driver, or cab master record. Foreign-key deletion rules should be chosen carefully.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
