273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 54 0 R
/T (Third Normal Form \(3NF\): Non-key attributes should depend on the key and not on other non-key attributes. Keeping customer, driver, and cab details in their own tables helps satisfy this principle. Removing or validating duplicated customer/driver IDs in RATING further improves consistency. Normalization should preserve the business meaning of the data. In particular, BOOKING.Driver_ID records the driver assigned to a booking, while CAB.Driver_ID may represent a current vehicle assignment; those are not necessarily the same fact if assignments can change over time.)
/E (Third Normal Form \(3NF\): Non-key attributes should depend on the key and not on other non-key attributes. Keeping customer, driver, and cab details in their own tables helps satisfy this principle. Removing or validating duplicated customer/driver IDs in RATING further improves consistency. Normalization should preserve the business meaning of the data. In particular, BOOKING.Driver_ID records the driver assigned to a booking, while CAB.Driver_ID may represent a current vehicle assignment; those are not necessarily the same fact if assignments can change over time.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [17]
>>
