450 0 obj
<<
/Title (Third Normal Form \(3NF\): Non-key attributes should depend on the key and not on other non-key attributes. Keeping customer, driver, and cab details in their own tables helps satisfy this principle. Removing or validating duplicated customer/driver IDs in RATING further improves consistency. Normalization should preserve the business meaning of the data. In particular, BOOKING.Driver_ID records the driver assigned to a booking, while CAB.Driver_ID may represent a current vehicle assignment; those are not necessarily the same fact if assignments can change over time.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 386 0 R
/Prev 499 0 R
>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<<
/Title (The main risks identified are the possible duplication of driver assignment data between CAB and BOOKING, duplicated customer and driver references in RATING, and the need to enforce the one-to-one relationships stated in the design. If these issues are not handled, the database may contain inconsistent assignments, ratings linked to the wrong participants, or multiple records where only one is intended.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 308 0 R
/Prev 387 0 R
/Next 452 0 R
>>
endobj
